{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929236-w-tf-2nd-edition-campaign-advice-consequences","id":929236,"title":"W:tF 2nd Edition Campaign Advice - Consequences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-10T08:49:57-07:00","id":929236,"title":"W:tF 2nd Edition Campaign Advice - Consequences","content":"Campaign Background: The players are a new Forsaken pack in San Fran which used to be a city controlled be a long established Pure pack. After a messy night where the Pure failed to recruit the players due to interception by an Oakland Forsaken pack who got stop tips from spirits for [reasons] the players decided to side with the Forsaken. The Pure were dealing with another problem at the time (Spider Hosts) and had a chunk of territory that was considered something of a problem to manage due to other supernatural involvement in the area [Chinatown], so they seeded the problem area to the new Forsaken pack while the Fire-Touched tried to play the long game and convert the pack over with gestures of good faith. &quot;You're new, you don't see the world how it truly is, you'll come around&quot; etc. That broken down when one of the Players murdered a bunch of the Ivory Claw's wolf-blooded and human pack members in death rage. The Pure kidnapped a pack members who was alone and the following situation developed.<br /> <br /> Immediate Background: Last session my players were negotiating with the Pure who had kidnapped one of their packmates. The Pure demanded their Ithaeur craft several fetishes for them, and that they give up the 'rights' to two of their wolf-blooded pack members. The pack refused, and so one of the pure who has a penchant for explosives threw a suitcase their way containing a bomb, and pulled out a detonater. While the leader (the Ivory Claw) attempted to use this to show the Forsaken they were not in a bargaining position the Rahu and Ithaeur quiet signaled to their Elodoth packmate (an NPC) to send the guy with the detonator into death rage so he couldn't pull the trigger. They did, a fight broke out. The Pure's scout/face got heavily injured and retreated, leaving the Pure two down (since their death rage pack mate was attacking them due to positioning). Seeing this the remaining sane packmates (The Ivory Claw and a Fire-Touched Shaman) fled the scene.<br /> <br /> Situation: The Ithaeur PC and Rahu PC were locked in combat with an unstable Pure Werewolf. The Pure began eating the Ithaeur and so the Ithaeur retaliated the same. Since this is a sin against harmony and also just generally disturbing the Flesh-leaning ex-Hunter Elodoth retreated further into a safe room and called her hunter friends to dispatch her packmate (who was in death rage and she perceived as an immediate threat to herself and some civilians in the room). The Pure dies, the Rahu bursts into the room to avoid going into death rage and they and the Elodoth hold the door. The Ithaeur isn't built for combat (and only killed the Pure because he also was not built for combat), so the two werewolves can hold the door for long time (the Rahu is very strong and durable). My questions are as follows.<br /> <br /> Question 1: In Death Rage if a werewolf sees prey flee into a safe room will they continue to attack the room until the death rage ends, or will they eventually get frustrated and look for easier prey?<br /> <br /> Question 2: The Pure werewolf that died had 5 dots in the totem merit. The Pure's totem is a huge threat to the Forsaken in the campaign, how do I maintain that threat now that it's lost 5 dots of power, or should I not?<br /> <br /> Sorry if that's all too much information, I wanted to have the context clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T11:52:02-07:00","id":929303,"title":"","content":"First: You attack anything that moves in death rage. Rabid animals will leave in frustration, but consider the senses Uratha have at their disposal. They have an universe of prey to pick off at their leisure in populated areas. Have the Rahu face the moral consequence to choosing to stay behind secure doors while his packmate went and murdered people, instead of being contained properly.<br /> <br /> Second? Wing it. If it's absolutely necessary that the totem keeps it's grip on the shadow, it keeps it.<br /> <br /> If the Elodoth is a packmate, calling his Hunters pals to deal with his Ithaeur packmate is betrayal of the pack of the highest order.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:01:57-07:00","id":929310,"title":"","content":"You can't really contain a werewolf in death rage, especially as a werewolf since just being in death rage sends other werewolves who can see you into death rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:43:29-07:00","id":929335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929236-w-tf-2nd-edition-campaign-advice-consequences?p=929310#post929310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't really contain a werewolf in death rage, especially as a werewolf since just being in death rage sends other werewolves who can see you into death rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I found it odd the other Pure and Forsaken didn't fall into death rage. Unless they all resisted. If the Uratha can't break through the safe room door, locking it in there would probably have contained it better than leaving it outside. Also, remember werewolves in death rage don't target each other.<br /> <br /> 1. Uratha have a lot of Merits and Gifts that would allow them to break through even a very secured, very heavy and durable door. Some activate for free during Death Rage, are you sure the Ithaeur wouldn't be able to break through? If so, after a couple of rounds of trying I would probably have the raging werewolf be distracted by activity outside. Perhaps someone called the police after all the noise. I do agree that calling hunters to deal with it would be seen as a betrayal.<br /> <br /> 2. I'd have the totem lose its power, but not immediately, more in a gradual way. This would give the Pure some more incentive to recruit, at the behest of their totem. Gathering up spiritual wolf-blooded and members of other Pure packs who want new opportunities, or just going out and grabbing ghost wolves and Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T13:05:20-07:00","id":929353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929236-w-tf-2nd-edition-campaign-advice-consequences?p=929335#post929335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I found it odd the other Pure and Forsaken didn't fall into death rage. Unless they all resisted.</div> </div> </div> </div>The shaman had a rite for it, the scout is actually an undercover Suthana Sua updated for 2e that doesn't trigger her madness rage off of death rages, the Ivory Claw, Rahu, Elodoth and Ithaeur all succeeded on their rolls until the Ithaeur's personal trigger was hit during the last part of the fight. Plus I have a house rule that all werewolves have one &quot;free turn&quot; the moment death rage starts to bail so that the game isn't a constant death rage frenzy that leads to the werewolves being found and killed in short order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929236-w-tf-2nd-edition-campaign-advice-consequences?p=929335#post929335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Uratha have a lot of Merits and Gifts that would allow them to break through even a very secured, very heavy and durable door. Some activate for free during Death Rage, are you sure the Ithaeur wouldn't be able to break through?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ithaeur's Gifts are as follows<br /> Crescent Moon 1 and 2<br /> Shadow Gaze<br /> Spirit Whispers<br /> Eyes of the Dead<br /> One Step Ahead<br /> <br /> The door is being braced by two werewolves, one slightly weaker and the other significantly stronger.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T13:13:41-07:00","id":929357,"title":"","content":"I think the differences in wasu-im and basu-im were basically there for werewolves to get some breathing room before things happen, outside of unique situations like an elodoth's one-a-chapter power.<br /> <br /> But it sounds like everything's going as it should be. I'd just have the Ithaeur rail against the door for a bit before being distracted by some other prey.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It does make me hope the next Forsaken book has more Auspice Gifts. And the police thing was just an example for high drama, you might just have it be drawn away by a passing motorist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-10-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T13:42:58-07:00","id":929368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929236-w-tf-2nd-edition-campaign-advice-consequences?p=929357#post929357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the differences in wasu-im and basu-im were basically there for werewolves to get some breathing room before things happen, outside of unique situations like an elodoth's one-a-chapter power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have read things wrong, but I believe that a death rage werewolf sends other werewolves immediately into death rage. So there's no soft rage buffer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T00:27:19-07:00","id":929602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929236-w-tf-2nd-edition-campaign-advice-consequences?p=929368#post929368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have read things wrong, but I believe that a death rage werewolf sends other werewolves immediately into death rage. So there's no soft rage buffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Falling into basu-im (hard rage) will cause any packmates (and packmates only) within 10 yards to fall into basu-im as well but only if they fail a resolve + composure roll, and it only happens when the packmate first falls into basu-im (though it happens every time a packmate does, even if they fell to basu-im as a result of another packmate falling into basu-im).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T04:43:35-07:00","id":929658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929236-w-tf-2nd-edition-campaign-advice-consequences?p=929602#post929602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Falling into basu-im (hard rage) will cause any packmates (and packmates only</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. There are still two schools of thought about whether Basu-Im's contagiousness is pack-only, or any werewolf within 10 yards. <br /> <br /> You can play it either way, but the choice will have a big impact on game style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}